# Authoritative for what `COPY . .` can see in the Dockerfile.
#
# The deploy uploads --source=web, so gcloud builds its ignore list from
# THIS directory's .gitignore, not the repo root's. The root file excludes
# build output as "web/.next-landing/" etc., which does not match once web/
# is the source root — so those directories were reaching the image.
#
# That is not cosmetic. Tailwind v4 scans the project for class names and
# skips git-ignored paths; inside the container nothing is git-ignored, so
# it parsed stale minified Next bundles, extracted garbage arbitrary-value
# classes from them and emitted invalid CSS. The build failed with
# "CssSyntaxError: Missed semicolon" pointing into globals.css.
#
# A .dockerignore is the durable guard because it does not depend on
# gcloud's upload behaviour or on which .gitignore happens to apply.

node_modules
.git

# Next build output, including the per-instance distDirs the e2e suite
# creates (playwright.config.ts gives each `next dev` its own, since Next
# refuses two dev servers sharing one .next/). These regenerate on every
# e2e run, so excluding them here is what keeps them out for good.
.next
.next-*
out
build

# Test output and local scratch
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
playwright/.cache
e2e/.scratch

.env*
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
